  "explanation": {
    "id": "81e17e6e-a3ae-46f1-9011-251e47e56052",
    "body": "To find the work, you evaluate the line integral $W = \\int_{C} \\vec{F} \\cdot d\\vec{r}$. However, notice that $\\vec{F} = \\langle x, y, z \\rangle$ is a conservative vector field because it is the gradient of the potential function $f(x, y, z) = \\frac{1}{2}(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)$.",
